From fd5b24ccfcc0b6334d0acf18212082c95fca08ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:28:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] fix(backend): RGB-D edge cases

- The runtime export leaves out a depth-only RealSense: the runtime reads
  color, and Studio's policies train without depth.
- The session view hides a camera's depth map only when the slot is a depth
  map, so a color camera named "x_depth" next to "x" stays visible.
- A depth range that keeps no depth is refused when a camera is saved, not
  when one is read: a stored row stays readable, and records unfiltered depth.
- Depth previews drop older versions of the same video and the least recently
  used beyond 2 GB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
